   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing community capacity to respond to HIV and AIDS in Western Equatoria state</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is 12 months HIV&amp;AIDS project targeting the church structures in the Diocese of Tombura-Yambio with the aim of strengthening its capacity in responding to the needs of PLWHA and the community through engaging in awareness raising on HIV&amp; AIDS at diocesan and county levels to increases risk perceptions in the selected parishes/county in order to reduce and prevent infection and Re-infection among the community. The project targets to train religious leaders, peer educators, PLWHA and other diocesan level actors; a total of 1055 people in the selected parishes/counties will be reached directly while an estimated 15,000 at risk population in the targeted parishes will indirectly be reached by the project through local media.
Following CDTY&#x2019;s three year project from April 2010 to March 2012 and its one year project from April 2013 &#x2013; March 2014, considerable achievements have been observed through an external evaluation and the diocese themselves. A number of lessons have been learnt, and despite the wide range of achievements made so far, there are still some significant challenges being faced. The design of this proposed project is therefore based on information collected during recent project monitoring visits conducted by CAFOD, Caritas Australia and CDTY. It will also continue to  addressed some of the gaps that were identified by the external evaluation report and the 2013 project.</narrative>
  </description>
